meta {
  name: Client testing
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/method/implementor.client_api.confirm_fix
  body: formUrlEncoded
  auth: inherit
}

body:form-urlencoded {
  ticket: 12ht7l2q84
  fixed: 1
  comment: Both users can see the Stock workspace now. Thanks!
  rating_overall: 5
  rating_quality: 4
  rating_communication: 5
  rating_response_time: 3
  ~customer: Hamza
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("has message", function () {
    expect(res.body).to.have.property("message");
  });

  test("ratings are saved", function () {
    expect(res.body.message.ratings.rating_overall).to.equal(5);
  });
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  The client confirms whether a resolved ticket is fixed.
  
  **Endpoint:** `POST /api/method/implementor.client_api.confirm_fix`  
  **Screen:** Ticket status → It is fixed / Still an issue
  
  > ⚠️ **Changes data** on the shared server. Use test records only.
  
  **Permission:** Signed-in client user (Client User or Client Admin). Only records of the user's own client company are returned.
  
  **Body fields (form-encoded):**
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Example | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `ticket` | string | yes | `12ht7l2q84` |  |
  | `fixed` | 1 / 0 | yes | `1` | 1 = It is fixed, 0 = Still an issue. |
  | `comment` | string | when fixed=0 | `...` | Also saved when `fixed=1`: it is added to the "Client confirmed the fix." comment. |
  | `rating_overall` | int 1–5 | no | `5` | Stars. |
  | `rating_quality` | int 1–5 | no | `4` | Fix quality. |
  | `rating_communication` | int 1–5 | no | `5` | |
  | `rating_response_time` | int 1–5 | no | `3` | |
  | `customer` | string | no | `Hamza` | Client company. Send only when `me.customers` has more than one entry. Disabled by default. |
  
  **Response (trimmed):**
  
  The updated ticket, in the same shape as **Ticket status**.

  ```json
  {
    "message": {
      "name": "12ht7l2q84",
      "status": "Closed",
      "needs_confirmation": false,
      "ratings": { "rating_overall": 5, "rating_quality": 4, "rating_communication": 5, "rating_response_time": 3 },
      "comments": [
        { "id": "...", "text": "Client confirmed the fix. Both users can see the Stock workspace now. Thanks!", "by": "Aisha Khan", "mine": true, "at": "..." }
      ],
      ...
    }
  }
  ```

  **Errors:**

  - **401:** Token missing, expired or invalid. Refresh once and retry, else sign out.
  - **403:** Not this client's record, or role not allowed.
  - **404:** Ticket not found.
  - **417:** Ticket not ready to confirm, comment missing when fixed=0, or a rating that isn't a whole number from 1 to 5.

  **Notes:**

  - Only works while the ticket is **Resolved** (`needs_confirmation: true`).
  - `fixed=1` → status becomes **Closed**. `fixed=0` → status goes back to **In Progress**.
  - Ratings are saved with either verdict. Leave a rating out (or empty) if the client skipped it; it comes back as `null`.
  - The comment is posted on the ticket with either verdict, after "Client confirmed the fix." or "Client reports it is still an issue."
}
